@page
@model PersonalTools.Pages.PrivacyModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }

<div class="container px-3 px-lg-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Last updated: 15 August 2026</p>
            <h1 class="page-title">Privacy notice</h1>
            <p class="page-subtitle section-spacing">How Personal Tools handles the information of its invited users.</p>
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Who is responsible</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Jake Hutson operates Personal Tools and is the data controller for the personal information described here. Contact: <a href="mailto:nerb162@gmail.com">nerb162@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Information collected</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Account email address, display name, securely hashed password, authentication session details (including expiry and browser user-agent), and—only if you choose to link it—your SteamID. Personal Tools also stores the content you deliberately add to the tools, including any CS2 match results you add manually or choose to import from Leetify.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Why and how it is used</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Account and session data are used to provide secure access to the service and protect accounts. Tool data is used to provide the feature you requested. The lawful basis is performance of the service requested by you, plus legitimate interests in keeping the private service secure and preventing misuse.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Audio Studio</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Audio Studio processes media files entirely in your browser. The selected file and resulting audio are not uploaded to, retained by, or accessible to Personal Tools.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Sharing and external services</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Personal information is not sold or used for advertising. It is processed only by the hosting and database providers needed to run Personal Tools. If you use Steam linking or the inventory lookup, Steam receives the request necessary to perform that feature. If you use the CS Match Tracker's "Fetch from Leetify" feature, the relevant SteamID (your own linked ID, or one you've entered for a match-tracking profile) is sent to Leetify's public match-history API at your request, so Personal Tools can retrieve and display your recent match results for you to choose from; only the matches you select are then stored. If you use tools that fetch public content, the relevant public service receives the request.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Retention and security</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Account and tool data are retained while the account remains active. Standard sessions expire after up to 24 hours; Remember me sessions expire after up to 14 days. Passwords are never stored in plain text. The service uses encrypted authentication cookies, server-side session checks, and access controls.</p></section>
                <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Your rights</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">You may ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information, or object to/restrict certain processing. Contact the controller above first. You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p></section>
                <section><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Cookies</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">See the <a asp-page="/Cookies">Cookies page</a> for details of the strictly necessary authentication and security cookies used by Personal Tools.</p></section>
            </div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
